{
  "suite": "pivot_cross_axis",
  "kind": "workbook",
  "description": "Two row fields crossed with a column field, and value columns that hold something other than a number. Both shapes were absent from the pivot corpus. Every earlier case has at most one axis populated on each side, so nothing pinned how a nested row hierarchy interacts with a column axis -- where the subtotal rows land, what the grand-total column spans, how an empty (Region, Product) pair renders under a column split. And no case put an error or a text value into a data field, so what Count and Sum do with one was engine inference rather than something Excel had been asked. The dataset is deliberately sparse: (South, Gadget) has no East-quarter row, so at least one cross-axis cell has no contributing record.",
